  "properties": {
    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Visualization Supervisor",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Marcus builds rough 3D scenes for an animation studio",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/eb551def59856a03411f61d319353bec-marcus.jpg",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "panels": [
      {
        "text": "**Career**: Visualization supervisor at an animation studio\n\n**Purpose**: Building rough 3D versions of scenes before the studio spends months animating them for real. Marcus moves cameras and characters around, renders quick previews, and reviews them with directors. Every minute he spends waiting on a render holds up the rest of the team.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/7ef02dfce9ce0ffaf20450229be0d90f-marcus-pane-1.jpg",
        "key": "undefined-42e502a3-e175-46f1-b693-dc6455a6cdd6",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "text": "**Budget**: $3,200\n\nCovers the entire system, including the operating system and peripherals.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/096bdd64118aec24a14064b5b4657f1d-marcus-pane-2.jpg",
        "key": "undefined-ff576ae3-1788-4ada-b264-7238ac25cc64"
      },
      {
        "text": "**Important Info**: Marcus's rendering software leans on the graphics card, not the processor, and he usually has several 3D programs open at once. Colors on his screen have to match the studio's final footage.\n\n**Preferences**:\n\n* The most powerful graphics card the budget allows, with as much video memory as possible\n* 64 GB of memory for running several 3D programs at the same time\n* A color-accurate monitor and a drawing tablet",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/3634f4136e0b8d5a089b59f675f47ac0-marcus-pane-3.jpg",
        "key": "undefined-035ce7ea-43d7-45a0-8f29-87a9fa949a04",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      }
    ],
    "use_links": "false"
  },
